{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1003","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Binary String Constructing"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given three integers $$$a$$$, $$$b$$$ and $$$x$$$. Your task is to construct a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n = a + b$$$ such that there are exactly $$$a$$$ zeroes, exactly $$$b$$$ ones and exactly $$$x$$$ indices $$$i$$$ (where $$$1 \\le i \\lt n$$$) such that $$$s_i \\ne s_{i + 1}$$$. It is guaranteed that the answer always exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, for the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01010"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" there are four indices $$$i$$$ such that $$$1 \\le i \\lt n$$$ and $$$s_i \\ne s_{i + 1}$$$ ($$$i = 1, 2, 3, 4$$$). For the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111001"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" there are two such indices $$$i$$$ ($$$i = 3, 5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that binary string is a non-empty sequence of characters where each character is either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text"